  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nThe upper high will slowly shift to the south and west Sunday and \nMonday and will have shifted far enough that isolated showers and \nthunderstorms will return during the afternoon and early evening \nboth days. The airmass over South-Central Texas will remain about \nthe same with low level flow from the east to southeast. \nTemperatures will be stagnant through the beginning of next week. It \nwill continue to feel like an endless summer rather than the start \nof fall. Tuesday models are showing the first real Pacific cold \nfront of the season moving into TX. This will bring chances for \nwidespread rain starting Tuesday. Models are not consistent on when \nthe front will move through and are extending rain chances into \nThursday. Northerly to northeasterly winds will bring cooler, drier \nair. Model forecast has trended a little warmer tonight, but \ntemperatures may get down to at least near normal.",
